+  {
+   "cell_type": "markdown",
+   "id": "9396dbcf",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "## Building subnetworks\n",
+    "\n",
+    "A `Subnetwork` groups a neural-mass `model`, an integration `scheme`, and a\n",
+    "node count.  `configure()` must be called before the subnetwork can be used\n",
+    "in a `NetworkSet`.\n",
+    "\n",
+    "**JansenRit** models a cortical column's excitatory/inhibitory loop and\n",
+    "spontaneously generates alpha-band (~10 Hz) oscillations.\n",
+    "\n",
+    "**ReducedSetFitzHughNagumo** is a population-level reduction of the classic\n",
+    "FitzHugh–Nagumo neuron.  It generates excitable or oscillatory dynamics\n",
+    "depending on its inputs.  `NetworkSet.observe()` sums over modes before\n",
+    "monitor output, so the default `number_of_modes = 3` works without\n",
+    "modification."
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": 3,
+   "id": "7997bb43",
+   "metadata": {
+    "execution": {
+     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-04-07T12:38:32.021627Z",
+     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-04-07T12:38:32.021513Z",
+     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-04-07T12:38:32.024614Z",
+     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-04-07T12:38:32.024123Z"
+    },
+    "title": "Build cortex subnetwork"
+   },
+   "outputs": [
+    {
+     "name": "stdout",
+     "output_type": "stream",
+     "text": [
+      "=== Cortex (JansenRit) ===\n",
+      "  state_variables : ('y0', 'y1', 'y2', 'y3', 'y4', 'y5')\n",
+      "  variables_of_interest: ('y0', 'y1', 'y2', 'y3')\n",
+      "  cvar (state-var indices used for coupling): [1 2]\n",
+      "  coupling-variable names: ['y1', 'y2']\n"
+     ]
+    }
+   ],
+   "source": [
+    "cortex = Subnetwork(\n",
+    "    name='cortex',\n",
+    "    model=JansenRit(),\n",
+    "    scheme=HeunDeterministic(dt=dt),\n",
+    "    nnodes=nnodes,\n",
+    ").configure()\n",
+    "\n",
+    "print(\"=== Cortex (JansenRit) ===\")\n",
+    "print(\"  state_variables :\", cortex.model.state_variables)\n",
+    "print(\"  variables_of_interest:\", cortex.model.variables_of_interest)\n",
+    "print(\"  cvar (state-var indices used for coupling):\", cortex.model.cvar)\n",
+    "print(\"  coupling-variable names:\", [cortex.model.state_variables[i]\n",
+    "                                     for i in cortex.model.cvar])"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": 4,
+   "id": "0573c4c2",
+   "metadata": {
+    "execution": {
+     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-04-07T12:38:32.025900Z",
+     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-04-07T12:38:32.025797Z",
+     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-04-07T12:38:32.030839Z",
+     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-04-07T12:38:32.030486Z"
+    },
+    "title": "Build thalamus subnetwork"
+   },
+   "outputs": [
+    {
+     "name": "stdout",
+     "output_type": "stream",
+     "text": [
+      "=== Thalamus (ReducedSetFitzHughNagumo) ===\n",
+      "  state_variables : ('xi', 'eta', 'alpha', 'beta')\n",
+      "  variables_of_interest: ('xi', 'alpha')\n",
+      "  cvar (state-var indices used for coupling): [0 2]\n",
+      "  coupling-variable names: ['xi', 'alpha']\n"
+     ]
+    }
+   ],
+   "source": [
+    "fhn_model = ReducedSetFitzHughNagumo()\n",
+    "# NetworkSet.observe() sums over modes before passing to monitors,\n",
+    "# so any number_of_modes (including the default of 3) works correctly.\n",
+    "\n",
+    "thalamus = Subnetwork(\n",
+    "    name='thalamus',\n",
+    "    model=fhn_model,\n",
+    "    scheme=HeunDeterministic(dt=dt),\n",
+    "    nnodes=nnodes,\n",
+    ").configure()\n",
+    "\n",
+    "print(\"=== Thalamus (ReducedSetFitzHughNagumo) ===\")\n",
+    "print(\"  state_variables :\", thalamus.model.state_variables)\n",
+    "print(\"  variables_of_interest:\", thalamus.model.variables_of_interest)\n",
+    "print(\"  cvar (state-var indices used for coupling):\", thalamus.model.cvar)\n",
+    "print(\"  coupling-variable names:\", [thalamus.model.state_variables[i]\n",
+    "                                     for i in thalamus.model.cvar])"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "markdown",
+   "id": "98dc3711",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "## Creating an inter-subnetwork projection\n",
+    "\n",
+    "An `InterProjection` carries activity from one subnetwork's *source cvar*\n",
+    "to another subnetwork's *target cvar*.  You name the variables using strings\n",
+    "drawn from `model.state_variables`:\n",
+    "\n",
+    "| argument | value | meaning |\n",
+    "|---|---|---|\n",
+    "| `source_cvar` | `'y1'` | JansenRit excitatory PSP — a coupling variable |\n",
+    "| `target_cvar` | `'xi'` | FHN slow variable — a coupling variable |\n",
+    "\n",
+    "The `weights` matrix has shape `(n_target_nodes, n_source_nodes)`.\n",
+    "Zero-length tract lengths are passed here because we are not modelling\n",
+    "conduction delays; `cv` and `dt` are required whenever `lengths` is given."
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": 5,
+   "id": "bbcdc0f7",
+   "metadata": {
+    "execution": {
+     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-04-07T12:38:32.032538Z",
+     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-04-07T12:38:32.032431Z",
+     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-04-07T12:38:32.035881Z",
+     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-04-07T12:38:32.035514Z"
+    },
+    "title": "Create InterProjection"
+   },
+   "outputs": [
+    {
+     "name": "stdout",
+     "output_type": "stream",
+     "text": [
+      "source_cvar index: [1]\n",
+      "target_cvar slot : [0]\n"
+     ]
+    }
+   ],
+   "source": [
+    "rng = np.random.RandomState(42)\n",
+    "weights_dense  = np.abs(rng.randn(nnodes, nnodes)) * 0.01  # (target, source)\n",
+    "weights_sparse = sp.csr_matrix(weights_dense)               # shape: (38, 38)\n",
+    "lengths_sparse = sp.csr_matrix((nnodes, nnodes))            # zero delays\n",
+    "\n",
+    "proj_ctx_to_thal = InterProjection(\n",
+    "    source=cortex,\n",
+    "    target=thalamus,\n",
+    "    source_cvar='y1',    # JansenRit coupling variable\n",
+    "    target_cvar='xi',    # FHN coupling variable\n",
+    "    weights=weights_sparse,\n",
+    "    lengths=lengths_sparse,\n",
+    "    cv=7.0,              # conduction velocity (mm/ms) — unused with zero lengths\n",
+    "    dt=dt,\n",
+    "    scale=0.1,           # global coupling strength\n",
+    ")\n",
+    "\n",
+    "print(\"source_cvar index:\", proj_ctx_to_thal.source_cvar)   # [1] (index of y1)\n",
+    "print(\"target_cvar slot :\", proj_ctx_to_thal.target_cvar)   # [0] (slot of xi)"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "markdown",
+   "id": "f50a536c",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "## Assembling the NetworkSet and running the simulation\n",
+    "\n",
+    "`NetworkSet` collects all subnetworks and inter-projections into one model.\n",
+    "`Simulator` owns the network and a list of TVB monitors.  After\n",
+    "`sim.configure()`, `sim.run(random_state=42)` draws initial conditions\n",
+    "from each model's `state_variable_range` using the given seed, then\n",
+    "advances the system for `simulation_length` milliseconds.\n",
+    "\n",
+    "The monitor returns one `(times, data)` tuple.  `data` has shape\n",
+    "`(n_time, total_vois, total_nodes, 1)` where VOIs and nodes from each\n",
+    "subnetwork are **concatenated in the order they appear in `subnets`**."
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": 6,
+   "id": "afd344af",
+   "metadata": {
+    "execution": {
+     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-04-07T12:38:32.037527Z",
+     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-04-07T12:38:32.037425Z",
+     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-04-07T12:38:32.039236Z",
+     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-04-07T12:38:32.038884Z"
+    },
+    "title": "Assemble NetworkSet"
+   },
+   "outputs": [],
+   "source": [
+    "nets = NetworkSet(\n",
+    "    subnets=[cortex, thalamus],   # cortex first → occupies VOI rows 0:4, nodes 0:38\n",
+    "    projections=[proj_ctx_to_thal],\n",
+    ")"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": 7,
+   "id": "bac1e510",
+   "metadata": {
+    "execution": {
+     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-04-07T12:38:32.040792Z",
